You have left this choice open, and each option gives a different result:
- "co-expression for each sample with edge p-values": BONOBO gives one gene-gene co-expression network per sample, estimated with a Bayesian model; optionally per-edge p-values per sample.
- "cohort-level TF-to-gene regulatory network from the same blood RNA-seq": PANDA gives one weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all the samples given; OTTER gives one weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all samples, fitted so that it agrees with the PPI network and gene co-expression.

